# Regenerable intermediates. Everything here is rebuilt by verify/prepare.py, verify/harness.html
# (served by verify/serve.py) and verify/cap.html, and none of it is evidence on its own. The evidence
# is the mp4s, the stills, metrics.json and verify/score.json, all of which ARE committed.
#
# It is 223 MB against ~10 MB of artifacts, so it is excluded deliberately rather than by accident.
# (gitignore has no trailing comments -- a pattern with one appended is a pattern that matches
# nothing, which is how this file failed the first time.)

# canonical trajectories plus the self-noise band, 58 MB
verify/base.npz

# the browser's rollouts, 4 MB each
verify/out/*.f32

# 486 captured PNG frames, 129 MB. The committed mp4s are built from these.
verify/out/cap/

# the water rework's frame sequences, same argument: cmp_water*.mp4 and the stills at the run root
# are built from these and ARE committed. The per-resolution cost JSONs next to it are NOT ignored --
# they are the measurement, not an intermediate.
verify/out/water/

# shared initial conditions, regenerated by prepare.py
verify/ic_*.f32
verify/ic_*.i32

# copied to shots/ at the run root, which IS committed
verify/shots/

# a stray Chromium profile in here breaks the data server's tree walk and 500s the dashboard
_*prof*/

# ephemeral live status
status.json
